Begin forwarded message:

*From:* "Glenn Ivey" <glenn@iveyforcongress.com>
*Date:* October 24, 2015 at 10:15:38 AM EDT
*To:* "Cheryl Mills" <cheryl.mills@gmail.com>
*Subject:* *Abolish the Benghazi Committee*
*Reply-To:* info@iveyforcongress.com


Dear Cheryl,

Watching the coverage of the Benghazi Committee's interrogation of
Secretary Clinton Thursday brought back a lot of memories from my time on
Capitol Hill. As Senator Paul Sarbanes' Legal Counsel, I sat on the
Whitewater Committee and had to put up with a lot of the same partisan
political games. And now, as was then, the Republican machine's obsession
with taking down the Clintons failed, backfired even.

In the process, all House Republicans seemed to achieve was wasting a lot
of taxpayer dollars on a partisan witch hunt.

So, in recognition of the House Republicans' failure to ruin Secretary
Clinton's chances at becoming our next President, *I am calling on Congress
to put an end to the partisan political games and abolish the Select
Committee on Benghazi.*

If you agree with me, then I encourage you to sign your name to our
petition *here
<https://act.myngp.com/el/5996192785785817088/420376881029056512?midqs=-7335800843033116672&recipientId=ZvrwnXz1N8mI3hBqTn1m92&email=cheryl.mills@gmail.com>*
and I will personally hand deliver it to Paul Ryan's desk when he becomes
Speaker.

They can only ignore us if they can't hear us. *Be heard. Sign your name
today
<https://act.myngp.com/el/5996192785785817088/420376881029056512?midqs=-7335800843033116672&recipientId=ZvrwnXz1N8mI3hBqTn1m92&email=cheryl.mills@gmail.com>*
.

Thank you for all that you do,

Glenn

